// Test: bugfixes/plugin_class_spec_cans_wiring
// Grammar: class_decl.can_clause · capability_decl · field_decl
// Semantic: This pin is the compiler-side companion to the ClassSpec `cans`
//   field added to typed_emission/batch_schema.rs in 0.33.111. Plugins
//   (frame.data v3.0.13+) will emit class specs with a `cans: ["Persist"]`
//   entry to declare that their model classes conform to capabilities they
//   also emit via `_emit_capability` (typed-emission §3.18). The compiler
//   converts that into `Class::capabilities` via class_to_ast, and the
//   resolver's Stage 5c populates vtable_descriptors from it.
//
// This pin exercises the equivalent HAND-WRITTEN shape: a class that has
//   both fields (making it non-utility, so has_fields=true) AND declares
//   `can Cap`, with a same-named method that satisfies the capability.
//   The combination previously wasn't well-covered by regression tests —
//   the SEM011 fix in 0.33.109 covered field-less capability classes; the
//   COM001 fix covered fielded-class + can-clause dispatch through a
//   capability-typed method receiver. This pin covers the direct
//   instance-method call path on a fielded class that also claims a
//   capability, which is the shape frame.data emits.
//
// If this ever regresses, plugin-emitted `data Widget:` bodies (which
//   frame.data v3.0.13+ will produce) will silently break end-to-end
//   even though the compiler accepts the `cans` field. The failure mode
//   is not a compile error — it's a runtime trap in the CallCapability
//   dispatch switch when no arm matches.
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.111
//
// Expected output:
//   true

start:
	Widget w = Widget()
	print(w.save().toString())

can Persist:
	boolean save()

class Widget can Persist
	public:
		integer id
	constructor()
		id = 7
	functions:
		public:
			boolean save()
				return true
